{"title":"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b Part ii","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2b\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2b</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2b\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">Problem 2b</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2b\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b2dbafd325dc8a379b8969f332a479e0bc9068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n, n + 1, n + 2, n + 3, n + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"17\" /> are five consecutive integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the average of these five consecutive integers is an odd integer, explain why <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be an odd integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b_Part_ii&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b_Part_i\" title=\"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b Part i\">part i</a>, the sum of the numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e07cf55ab45e94138dfd68d66f186ce208c76d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5n + 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, this would make the average <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773c6ad90df03d3d8dd6767a6b8413698add6a13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5n + 10}{5} = n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have realized that the numbers were consecutive, so the median would be the same as the average. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers (an odd amount), so the median is just the middle number, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The only way for the sum of two integers to be odd is if one is odd while the other is even. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is even, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be odd.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017223300\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 44/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 234/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1604/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.540      1 -total\n 53.53%    8.319      1 2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n 45.26%    7.033      1 2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with 